        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en"># Included processes\nElectricity mix from wind power in Europe.\nThe mix consists of 87% from onshore wind farms and 13% from offshore wind farms, reflecting a total electrictiy generation of 420 TWh from onshore wind farms and 61.8 TWh from offshore wind farms in 2024 (source: ENTSO-E).\n\nThe considered contributions from different wind turbine sizes to the electrcity generation mix are:\n50% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &lt; 3 MW (modelled using 2.3 MW onshore wind turbine)\n22% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 3 MW and &lt; 4 MW (modelled using 3.4 MW onshore wind turbines)\n10% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 4 MW and &lt; 5.5 MW (modelled with 4.5 MW onshore wind turbines)\n5% from onshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 5.5 MW (modelled with 6.4 MW onshore wind turbines)\n5% from offshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &lt; 7 MW (modelled with 5 MW offshore wind turbines)\n7% from offshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 7 MW and &lt; 12 MW (modelled with 10 MW offshore wind turbines)\n1% from offshore wind turbines with nominal capacities &gt;= 12 MW (modelled with 15 MW offshore wind turbines)\n</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
